= Genetics =

== Overview ==
'''Genetics''' is the branch of biology concerned with heredity, genes, genetic variation, and how inherited information contributes to biological traits.

Genetics studies how biological information is transmitted and varied across generations and cells. It includes inheritance patterns, gene function, mutation, recombination, genotype–phenotype relationships, and interactions between genetic variation and environment.

Modern genetics spans molecular, population, quantitative, developmental, and medical approaches. A gene can influence a trait without being its sole cause; many traits arise from multiple genetic and environmental factors.

Genetics overlaps with genomics but is not identical to it. Genomics emphasizes genome-scale organization and interaction across many genes and other genomic elements.

== Boundaries ==
* genetics ≠ genomics
* gene influence ≠ single-gene determinism
* heritability ≠ immutability

